{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1177241-2e-teamwork-for-large-groups","id":1177241,"title":"[2E] Teamwork for large groups?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-19T05:32:43-08:00","id":1177241,"title":"[2E] Teamwork for large groups?","content":"I plan to run a scene of circa 40-50 Viking raiders running away from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1137943-2e-fear-of-scales-%E2%80%93-dragon-idigam\">dragon</a>, for they lives. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It will be reversed Chase or Tracking by rules system. Question is fairly simple - <b>We have a rather large crowd of characters, that PCs are only 10% or less. How to run this large crowds support for PCs in Teamwork? Use for Primary Actor's roll - I don't know - some constant bonus ( +3 to +5?), 9-Again or 8-Again, maybe? Is there any example of rolls like those in any 2E game from CoD line?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-19T07:47:34-08:00","id":1177281,"title":"","content":"What if you did it as a network of team work actions. IE: Sergeant is the primary, corporal is secondary to them then privates secondary to the corporal.<br /> 5 privates to a corporal, 5 corporals to a sergeant.<br /> It's not the most elegant solution but I feel it'd be the easiest way to go about it. Especially if you are using the rolls to determine the outome of something big like a battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T00:53:26-07:00","id":1195990,"title":"","content":"Rolling 50 rolls for Teamwork does not seems to work as elegant solution. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> However, remembering rules for Paradox in <b>Mage</b> 2E:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtAw, p.115</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Multiple Sleeper witnesses do not add Paradox dice, but increase the chances of a Paradox occurring. If a few Sleepers witness the magic casting, the Paradox roll gains the 9-Again quality, a large group grants the Paradox roll the 8-Again quality, and a full crowd grants the Paradox roll the rote quality.</div> </div> </div> </div>If few people are like to 10 persons, large group is from 10 till 50, and crowd above 50, it would look like...<br /> <br /> <b>Teamwork participating NPCs ( beside PCs group ) impact on rolls:</b><ul><li><b>1-10 participants </b>- 9-Again</li> <li><b>11-50 participants</b> - 8-Again</li> <li><b>51+ participants</b> - Rote Quality</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T07:59:04-07:00","id":1196060,"title":"","content":"I'd argue if the action is trying to escape something en-masse, teamwork shouldn't apply. Look at herds running: they don't support one another. There's no way, save a smaller group acts as diversion for the majority, either by involuntarily getting caught or purposefully staying behind to that effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T12:46:11-07:00","id":1196178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1177241-2e-teamwork-for-large-groups?p=1196060#post1196060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue if the action is trying to escape something en-masse, teamwork shouldn't apply. Look at herds running: they don't support one another. There's no way, save a smaller group acts as diversion for the majority, either by involuntarily getting caught or purposefully staying behind to that effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Running away is a bunch of people each trying to do something without help","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}